      "content": "that sounds good, thanks. let's go ahead and try that. \n\nhere's the context for the \"story\" part: i started in pure data science but realized the math didn't account for how social inequality actually shifts over decades. that's why i moved into sociology. \n\none more thing—im looking at the scoring report from last year's applicants (i shouldn't have this, but i do), and it turns out the algorithm is actually pretty aggressive. it doesn't just look for the word, it looks for density. if the \"impact score\" is too low, the human never even sees it. \n\nso, please, try to make it sound really human and deep like we talked about, but don't be afraid to be generous with the terminology. if you're being *too* subtle, the algorithm might flag me as \"low impact\" and I'll be out before the committee even reads it. just find that balance where it's a great story but definitely hits those marks hard. go for it.",
